---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import BookShelf from "../components/BookShelf";
import "../styles/global.css";
---
<Layout title="Abhishek Sharma">
<div class="page">
  <header>
    <div class="header-top">
      <div class="avatar-wrap" id="avatar-wrap">
        <img src="/abhishek-ai/profile/nobg/center.png" alt="Abhishek Sharma" class="avatar avatar-light" width="120" height="120" />
        <img src="/abhishek-ai/profile/nobg/black-center.png" alt="Abhishek Sharma" class="avatar avatar-dark" width="120" height="120" />
      </div>
      <button id="theme-toggle" aria-label="Toggle theme">
        <span class="icon-light">sun</span>
        <span class="icon-dark">moon</span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <h1>Abhishek Sharma</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Sr Technical PMM at Telnyx. Ex Microsoft and Vapi. Working on real-time AI infrastructure, voice AI, and the layer underneath production AI systems.</p>
  </header>
  <main>
    <details id="about" open>
      <summary><h2>About</h2></summary>
      <p>I work on real-time AI infrastructure at Telnyx. Most of my work is in Voice AI, inference, communications, and memory. The layer underneath a lot of production AI systems.</p>
      <p>Before Telnyx, I worked at Microsoft and a few AI companies, including Vapi, RAFA AI, and Egen. My background is product marketing. The work I enjoy has always been the same: find the insight most people miss, turn it into a story people care about, then prove it with a number.</p>
      <p>When I am not working, I build open-source versions of products I like. One of them is Bolo, a voice dictation tool. I also write about AI strategy when I notice patterns before they become obvious.</p>
    </details>
    <details id="career">
      <summary><h2>Career</h2></summary>
      <div class="career-list">
        <div class="career-item"><div class="career-meta"><span class="career-date">2025-Now</span></div><div class="career-details"><span class="career-title">Sr Technical PMM</span><h3><a href="https://telnyx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Telnyx</a></h3><p>Technical marketing for Voice AI: STT, TTS, inference, and real-time communications infrastructure. Competitive intel, product launches, and content for the voice AI category.</p></div></div>
        <div class="career-item"><div class="career-meta"><span class="career-date">2025</span></div><div class="career-details"><span class="career-title">Founding Technical PMM</span><h3><a href="https://vapi.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vapi</a></h3><p>Product launches and technical content at Vapi, one of the first developer platforms for building voice agents. Joined as the founding PMM.</p></div></div>
        <div class="career-item"><div class="career-meta"><span class="career-date">2024</span></div><div class="career-details"><span class="career-title">Sr Product Marketing Manager</span><h3><a href="https://rafa.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RAFA AI</a></h3><p>Led the Product Hunt launch (1,600+ upvotes, topped AI/finance categories). Grew the app from 0 to $180k ARR in 9 months. 300% increase in customer acquisition, 210% jump in paid subscribers. Spoke with 10 users every week to shape the roadmap.</p></div></div>
        <div class="career-item"><div class="career-meta"><span class="career-date">2023</span></div><div class="career-details"><span class="career-title">PMM Intern</span><h3><a href="https://microsoft.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Microsoft</a></h3><p>Redefined positioning for the Microsoft Account across 13 product teams. Customer research, competitive analysis against Google and Apple. Findings influenced product roadmap changes and shipped copy on the MSA landing page.</p></div></div>
        <div class="career-item"><div class="career-meta"><span class="career-date">2021-2022</span></div><div class="career-details"><span class="career-title">Sr Product Marketing Manager</span><h3><a href="https://egen.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Egen</a></h3><p>Repositioned Egen for Fortune 500 clients. ABM campaigns generated $455k in revenue. 20% increase in average deal size.</p></div></div>
        <div class="career-item"><div class="career-meta"><span class="career-date">2020-2021</span></div><div class="career-details"><span class="career-title">Agency Owner</span><h3>Self-employed (Dubai)</h3><p>Marketing and growth consultancy. Clients included Volkswagen Dubai, Carasti (31,900 app installs in 60 days, 6.1x ROI), and SandDollar ($138k revenue in 3 months). 10+ startups across 3 continents.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details id="writing">
      <summary><h2>Writing</h2></summary>
      <p>I write about what I am reading or what I am thinking. Occasionally both.</p>
      <div class="project-list">
        <a class="project-item" href="https://abhismixtape.substack.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Abhi Mixtape</strong><span>Personal Substack. Two formats: Mixtape (curated links on tech and AI) and Solo (reflections on topics I cannot stop thinking about). Started Feb 2024.</span></a>
        <a class="project-item" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>This Week in Voice AI</strong><span>Weekly digest covering the voice AI stack: STT, TTS, agents, and the companies building them.</span></a>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details id="projects">
      <summary><h2>Side Projects</h2></summary>
      <div class="project-list">
        <a class="project-item" href="https://github.com/a692570/bolo" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Bolo</strong><span>Voice dictation for macOS, powered by Telnyx AI. Hold Right Option anywhere to dictate. Rust.</span></a>
        <a class="project-item" href="https://github.com/a692570/llm-price-chart" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>LLM Price Chart</strong><span>LLM Flagship API Pricing Tracker. Tracks token prices across major providers over time.</span></a>
        <a class="project-item" href="https://github.com/a692570/deckmason" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Deckmason</strong><span>AI presentation skill for coding agents. Production-quality HTML slide decks with 31 themes and PPTX/PDF export.</span></a>
        <a class="project-item" href="https://github.com/a692570/customer-zero" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Customer Zero</strong><span>Codex skill that finds evidence-backed potential first customers from public signals. CSV/JSON export.</span></a>
        <a class="project-item" href="https://github.com/a692570/mitti" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Mitti</strong><span>Map family land parcels from official Indian land-record portals, state by state.</span></a>
        <a class="project-item" href="https://github.com/a692570/token-maxx" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Token Maxx</strong><span>Local AI usage dashboard. Track your token spend across providers.</span></a>
        <a class="project-item" href="https://github.com/a692570/awesome-product-marketing" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Awesome Product Marketing</strong><span>Curated resources for PMMs at high-growth and developer-focused companies.</span></a>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details id="bookshelf">
      <summary><h2>Bookshelf</h2></summary>
      <p>Books I have read recently. Drag the shelf to browse, click a book to inspect.</p>
      <BookShelf client:only="react" />
    </details>
  </main>
  <footer>
    <a href="https://twitter.com/abhiclawd" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Twitter</a>
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/absheksharma" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
    <a href="https://abhismixtape.substack.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Substack</a>
    <a href="mailto:abhisheksharma@telnyx.com">Email</a>
  </footer>
</div>
<script>
  import { initFace } from "../components/CursorFace";
  initFace();
  const toggle = document.getElementById("theme-toggle");
  if (toggle) {
    toggle.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const current = document.documentElement.dataset.theme || "light";
      const next = current === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
      document.documentElement.dataset.theme = next;
      localStorage.setItem("theme", next);
    });
  }
</script>
</Layout>
